{"id":"4a86347682d8580a","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-reflexive.md","title":"Reflexive Relation","display":"df-reflexive — Reflexive Relation","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-reflexive","aliases":["58-df-reflexive"],"display":"df-reflexive — Reflexive Relation","depends_on":["[[../batch18/58-df-relation.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-set.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-reflexive"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-reflexive</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-reflexive — Reflexive Relation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"7ccfc8c88f29968a\" href=\"?note=7ccfc8c88f29968a\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-relation.md\">../batch18/58-df-relation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"65d9a1e690c32aad\" href=\"?note=65d9a1e690c32aad\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-set.md\">../batch12/58-df-set.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R,A\\in V\">\\(R,A\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Set}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Set}_S\\)</span> (set predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"65d9a1e690c32aad\" href=\"?note=65d9a1e690c32aad\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-set.md\">../batch12/58-df-set.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Rel}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Rel}_S\\)</span> (binary-relation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"7ccfc8c88f29968a\" href=\"?note=7ccfc8c88f29968a\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-relation.md\">../batch18/58-df-relation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Reflexive}_S,\\mathrm{Reflexive}\">\\(\\mathrm{Reflexive}_S,\\mathrm{Reflexive}\\)</span> (reflexive-relation predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflexive} \\vdash \\mathrm{Reflexive}_S(R,A)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Set}_S(A)\\land \\mathrm{Rel}_S(R,A,A)\\land \\forall x\\in A\\;(\\langle x,x\\rangle\\in R)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflexive} \\vdash \\mathrm{Reflexive}_S(R,A)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Set}_S(A)\\land \\mathrm{Rel}_S(R,A,A)\\land \\forall x\\in A\\;(\\langle x,x\\rangle\\in R)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflexive\\text{-}compatible} \\vdash \\mathrm{Reflexive}(R,A)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Reflexive}_S(R,A)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflexive\\text{-}compatible} \\vdash \\mathrm{Reflexive}(R,A)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Reflexive}_S(R,A)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reflexivity is relative to the stated carrier <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span>; the same graph can fail to be reflexive on a larger carrier.</li>\n<li>The compatibility name <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Reflexive}\">\\(\\mathrm{Reflexive}\\)</span> is the contract used by the poset and potentialist-frame atoms.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch18/58-df-relation.md","status":"resolved","id":"7ccfc8c88f29968a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../bat